  "content": "<!-- wp:cil/hero {\"sub\":\"Two experienced practitioners who have trained UK and International doctors. Local anaesthetic every time.\",\"html\":\"\",\"facts\":[{\"text\":\"<b>4.9</b> from 2,092 Google reviews\",\"icon\":\"google\"},{\"text\":\"CQC registered, rated Good\",\"icon\":\"shield\"},{\"text\":\"<b>Weekday and Weekend appointments available</b>\",\"icon\":\"clock\"},{\"text\":\"Free street parking. Outside the Congestion Charge zone\",\"icon\":\"pin\"}],\"eyebrow\":\"CQC registered · Edgware, North-West London\",\"title\":\"Dedicated Circumcision Clinic in London\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book online\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/book/\",\"phoneLabel\":\"Call 020 8951 3794\",\"phoneUrl\":\"tel:+442089513794\",\"showFacts\":true} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/groups {\"items\":[{\"image\":\"home/babies-card-720.webp\",\"imageAlt\":\"\",\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/babies/\",\"title\":\"Babies and toddlers\",\"age\":\"Best under one month old\",\"price\":\"From £200\",\"cta\":\"Baby circumcision, from £200\",\"blurb\":\"Circumcision is commonly carried out using the Plastibell or Circumplast ring method. For young babies, the procedure itself is usually less than 10 minutes and no stitches are required with the ring method. Bath him straight away.\"},{\"image\":\"home/children-card-720.webp\",\"imageAlt\":\"\",\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/children/\",\"title\":\"Children and teenagers\",\"age\":\"3-17 years old\",\"price\":\"From £300\",\"cta\":\"Circumcision for boys, from £300\",\"blurb\":\"Older children are commonly treated using the forceps-guided traditional method with thermal cautery resulting in minimal bleeding. We explain the procedure in an age-appropriate way and provide parents with detailed aftercare instructions.\"},{\"image\":\"home/adults-card-720.webp\",\"imageAlt\":\"\",\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\",\"title\":\"Adults\",\"age\":\"Eighteen and over\",\"price\":\"From £680\",\"cta\":\"Adult circumcision, from £680\",\"blurb\":\"We provide adult circumcision for religious, cultural, personal and medical reasons, including foreskin problems such as phimosis, paraphimosis, balanitis and BXO. We also assess patients seeking re-circumcision or revision procedures.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/trust-strip {\"googleLogo\":true,\"cqcWidget\":true,\"googleLinkLabel\":\"View on Google Maps\",\"cqcLinkLabel\":\"CQC Good\",\"items\":[{\"n\":\"4.9\",\"l\":\"From 2,092 Google reviews, checked on 2 September 2026.\"},{\"n\":\"40+\",\"l\":\"Years of combined experience between our two practitioners, in the UK and abroad. They both train doctors from UK and abroad.\"},{\"n\":\"CQC\",\"l\":\"Registered with the Care Quality Commission and rated Good at previous inspections.\",\"linkLabel\":\"Read the report\",\"linkUrl\":\"https://www.cqc.org.uk/location/1-470883883\"},{\"n\":\"6\",\"l\":\"Languages spoken here: English, Arabic, Urdu, Hindi, Punjabi and Turkish.\"}],\"googleLinkUrl\":\"https://www.google.com/maps?cid=3913365297956493985\",\"cqcLinkUrl\":\"https://www.cqc.org.uk/location/1-470883883\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/reviews {\"eyebrow\":\"Reviews\",\"checkedNote\":\"Checked on 2 September 2026, and refreshed quarterly so the number here is the number on the profile.\",\"body\":\"\",\"platforms\":[{\"label\":\"Google Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://www.google.com/maps?cid=3913365297956493985\",\"icon\":\"google\"},{\"label\":\"Trustpilot\",\"url\":\"https://uk.trustpilot.com/review/www.circumcisioninlondon.co.uk\",\"icon\":\"trustpilot\"},{\"label\":\"Yell\",\"url\":\"https://www.yell.com/biz/circumcision-in-london-edgware-6864473/\",\"icon\":\"yell\"}],\"testimonialsLabel\":\"Read patient testimonials\",\"testimonialsUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/testimonials/\",\"videosHeading\":\"\",\"videos\":[{\"title\":\"Babies\",\"mediaKey\":\"testimonials/videos/img-4542.mp4\",\"posterKey\":\"testimonials/posters/img-4542.jpg\"},{\"title\":\"Children\",\"mediaKey\":\"testimonials/videos/img-4967.mp4\",\"posterKey\":\"testimonials/posters/img-4967.jpg\"},{\"title\":\"Adults\",\"mediaKey\":\"testimonials/videos/img-5430.mp4\",\"posterKey\":\"testimonials/posters/img-5430.jpg\"}],\"videosCtaLabel\":\"View all video testimonials\",\"videosCtaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/video-testimonials/\",\"quotes\":[{\"name\":\"Mustafa Butt\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision, three weeks old\",\"quote\":\"The receptionist explained the procedure clearly and put us at ease straight away. The doctor was thorough and professional, explained everything beforehand, and stayed calm and reassuring throughout. He took the time to go through the aftercare in detail.\"},{\"name\":\"Wajahat Murtaza\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision\",\"quote\":\"Smooth and efficient from start to finish. Dr Haidar is professional and experienced, we were given all the information we needed, and a follow-up call was made as well, which is a nice thing to do. The ring came off after a week and my son is doing well.\"},{\"name\":\"Sara Salmanpour\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision, two months old\",\"quote\":\"As first-time parents we were naturally anxious, but the team made us feel completely at ease. The doctor explained the procedure in detail and answered every concern with patience. They gave us the option to contact them any time afterwards, which was a huge relief.\"}],\"heading\":\"4.9 from 2,092 Google reviews\",\"stars\":\"★★★★★\",\"stats\":[{\"n\":\"2,092\",\"l\":\"Google reviews, at 4.9 out of 5.\"},{\"n\":\"Word of\\nmouth\",\"l\":\"How most of our patients find us: family and friends who came first.\"},{\"n\":\"Years\\napart\",\"l\":\"Families returning whenever there is a new son in the family.\"},{\"n\":\"CQC Good\",\"l\":\"Rated at previous inspections by the regulator.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/home-clinic-introduction -->\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-sky\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"clinic-introduction\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-sky\" id=\"clinic-introduction\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cil-split-copy\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group cil-split-copy\"><!-- wp:cil/rich-html {\"html\":\"\\u003cspan class=\\u0022caps eyebrow\\u0022\\u003eAbout our clinic\\u003c/span\\u003e\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-home-intro\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-home-intro\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision in London at Beverley Clinic provides male circumcision for infants, babies, children, teenagers, boys and adult men. Our two circumcision practitioners have more than 40 years of combined experience in the UK and abroad and have carried out thousands of successful circumcisions across all age groups.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We understand that choosing circumcision for yourself or your child is an important decision. Our aim is to explain the procedure clearly, answer your questions and support you from the initial enquiry through to aftercare and healing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision may be requested for religious (such as Muslim and Jewish), cultural, personal or medical reasons. Every patient is assessed individually, and the method used depends on age, anatomy and clinical circumstances.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/figure {\"name\":\"clinic-exterior\",\"ratio\":\"4-3\",\"caption\":\"40+ years combined practitioner experience\",\"alt\":\"Beverley Clinic illuminated window sign at 78 Beverley Drive, Edgware, at night.\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-home-intro\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-home-intro\"><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Circumcision for babies, children, teenagers and adults</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Local anaesthetic used for circumcisions, with the area checked before the procedure begins</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Written aftercare information and preparation videos</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Next-day follow-up call</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Free follow-up appointments during the healing period</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>GP letter available to update medical records</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>School or work letters available where appropriate</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>English, Arabic, Urdu, Hindi, Punjabi and Turkish spoken</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section --><!-- /wp:cil/home-clinic-introduction -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/home-meet-practitioners -->\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"meet-practitioners\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"meet-practitioners\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Meet our practitioners\",\"lede\":\"\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Dr Haidar Al-Ali and Dr Samir Al-Ali are the clinic's circumcision practitioners. They have more than 40 years of combined experience in the UK and abroad and have carried out thousands of circumcisions across different age groups.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"24px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\" style=\"margin-top:24px\"><!-- wp:button --><div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/team/\">Meet the practitioners</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/video-grid {\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Meet our Circumcision Practitioners\",\"description\":\"Our two practitioners have more than 40 years of combined experience in the UK and abroad and have carried out thousands of circumcisions across different age groups.\",\"duration\":\"0:27\",\"mediaKey\":\"about/meet-our-circumcision-practitioners.mp4\",\"poster\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/wp-content/themes/circumcision-london/assets/images/about/meet-our-circumcision-practitioners.jpg\",\"mp4\":\"\",\"posterId\":0,\"mp4Id\":0}],\"layout\":\"list\",\"itemLevel\":2,\"showHead\":false} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n<!-- /wp:cil/home-meet-practitioners -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/home-additional-sections -->\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"why-patients-come-to-us\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"why-patients-come-to-us\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Why patients come to us\",\"lede\":\"\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"icon\":\"award\",\"title\":\"Specialist focus\",\"body\":\"Circumcision is a core part of our day-to-day clinical work rather than an occasional procedure. Our practitioners have extensive experience in circumcision and have also trained doctors from the UK and abroad in circumcision techniques and patient care.\"},{\"icon\":\"users\",\"title\":\"All ages\",\"body\":\"We provide circumcision for babies, toddlers, children, teenagers and adults, using techniques appropriate to the patient's age, anatomy and individual circumstances.\"},{\"icon\":\"refresh\",\"title\":\"Continuity of care\",\"body\":\"Our care does not end when the procedure is finished. Patients and parents receive preparation information before treatment, detailed written aftercare afterwards, a next-day follow-up call and ongoing support throughout the healing period.\"},{\"icon\":\"heart\",\"title\":\"Trusted by patients and parents\",\"body\":\"Much of our work comes through word-of-mouth recommendations from previous patients and families. We are proud that patients continue to recommend Beverley Clinic to their friends, relatives and communities.\"},{\"icon\":\"star\",\"title\":\"Thousands of patient reviews\",\"body\":\"We have received thousands of 5 star reviews from patients and parents who have used our service. Read about their experiences on Google, Trustpilot and Yell.com.\"},{\"icon\":\"map\",\"title\":\"Convenient North-West London location\",\"body\":\"Our clinic is located in Edgware, North-West London, with good public transport links and free street parking nearby at all times.\"}],\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false,\"bleed\":true} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split split--bleed\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cil-split-copy\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group cil-split-copy\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group \"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Circumcision for medical reasons\",\"display\":\"d-1\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision is not only performed for religious (Islam and Judaism), cultural or personal reasons. It can also be recommended to treat certain medical conditions affecting the foreskin or penis. We assess each patient individually and will discuss whether circumcision or an alternative treatment is most appropriate.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/figure {\"name\":\"sterilisation\",\"ratio\":\"4-3\",\"alt\":\"An autoclave used to sterilise instruments at the clinic.\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Phimosis (tight foreskin)\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003ePhimosis occurs when the foreskin is too tight to retract comfortably over the head of the penis (glans).\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about phimosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Recurrent balanitis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBalanitis is inflammation of the head of the penis (glans), which can cause redness, soreness, irritation and discomfort.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/balanitis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about balanitis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"BXO / lichen sclerosis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBXO (balanitis xerotica obliterans), also known as male genital lichen sclerosis, can affect the foreskin and cause whitening, thickening, scarring and progressive tightness.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/bxo/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about BXO / lichen sclerosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Paraphimosis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eParaphimosis occurs when the foreskin has been pulled back behind the head of the penis and cannot be returned to its normal position.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/paraphimosis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about paraphimosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Tight frenulum\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe frenulum is the band of tissue on the underside of the penis connecting the foreskin to the head of the penis (glans).\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/procedures/frenuloplasty/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about frenuloplasty and tight frenulum →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Buried penis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eA buried or hidden penis is where some or all of the penis is concealed within the surrounding pubic tissue.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/buried-penis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about buried penis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}],\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-sky\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-sky\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":true,\"bleed\":true} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split reverse split--bleed\"><!-- wp:cil/figure {\"name\":\"treatment-room\",\"ratio\":\"4-3\",\"alt\":\"The clean, white treatment room at the Edgware clinic, with a treatment couch.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cil-split-copy\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group cil-split-copy\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group \"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Circumcision methods used at our London clinic\",\"display\":\"d-1\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text cil-section-lede\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text cil-section-lede\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>There are several ways to perform a circumcision, and no single method is suitable for every patient. At Beverley Clinic, we select the circumcision technique according to the patient&#039;s age, anatomy, reason for circumcision and findings on examination.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our practitioners have extensive experience in circumcising babies, children, teenagers and adults and use different techniques according to the individual patient.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Plastibell and Circumplast circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor babies and younger children, we commonly use the Plastibell or Circumplast ring method where clinically suitable.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/babies/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about baby circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Forceps-guided circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor older children, teenagers and adults, we commonly use a forceps-guided circumcision technique with thermal cautery.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/children/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about circumcision for children 3+ →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about adult circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Re-circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eRe-circumcisions often means less skin to work with compared to an uncircumcised patient. Hence, we often have to use a freehand technique.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/re-circumcision/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about re-circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}],\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section --><!-- /wp:cil/home-additional-sections -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/process {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Next steps\",\"lede\":\"\",\"items\":[{\"h\":\"Contact us\",\"p\":\"Ask questions by telephone, WhatsApp or the website enquiry form.\"},{\"h\":\"Preparation\",\"p\":\"We send you written and video information to prepare you on what to bring, what to expect on the day and the expected aftercare following the circumcision.\"},{\"h\":\"Procedure\",\"p\":\"Local anaesthetic is given and the area is checked before the procedure begins.\"},{\"h\":\"Aftercare\",\"p\":\"You leave with written instructions. We contact you the following day to answer any further questions you may have and offer follow-up appointments during healing if needed.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/intro {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Location\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBeverley Clinic, 78 Beverley Drive, Edgware, HA8 5NE. The clinic is in North-West London with nearby public transport links and plenty of free street parking. Queensbury Underground station (8 mins walk) on the Jubilee line and Burnt Oak station on the Northern line (20 mins walk) are both nearby.\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"mediaType\":\"map\",\"mapEmbedUrl\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"btn1Label\":\"Book online\",\"btn1Url\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/book/\",\"btn2Label\":\"Call us\",\"btn2Url\":\"tel:+442089513794\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"anchor\":\"our-clinics\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"our-clinics\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Our clinics\",\"heading\":\"Other locations\",\"lede\":\"The London clinic in Edgware can be booked online. Luton, Southampton and Birmingham are booked by telephone on 0330 133 4535.\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Luton\",\"title\":\"Luton\",\"html\":\"<p style=\\\"margin-top:12px\\\">Liverpool Road Health Centre<br>9 Mersey Place<br>Luton<br>LU1 1HH</p><p>Telephone: <a href=\\\"tel:+443301334535\\\">0330 133 4535</a></p>\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Luton clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/luton-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Southampton\",\"title\":\"Southampton\",\"html\":\"<p style=\\\"margin-top:12px\\\">Beverley Clinic<br>Eastleigh Health Centre<br>Eastleigh SO50 9AG</p><p>Telephone: <a href=\\\"tel:+443301334535\\\">0330 133 4535</a></p>\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Southampton clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/southampton-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Birmingham\",\"title\":\"Birmingham\",\"html\":\"<p style=\\\"margin-top:12px\\\">Beverley Clinic<br>Soho Health Centre<br>Louise Road<br>Birmingham B21 9RY</p><p>Telephone: <a href=\\\"tel:+443301334535\\\">0330 133 4535</a></p>\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Birmingham clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/birmingham-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"}],\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":2} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/cta-band {\"title\":\"If you have further questions\",\"text\":\"<p>If you have further questions, you can either <a href=\\\"tel:+442089513794\\\">call us</a> or <a href=\\\"#request-callback\\\">request for us to call you back</a>. You can also send us an <a href=\\\"mailto:info@circumcisioninlondon.co.uk\\\">email enquiry</a> or speak to us via <a href=\\\"https://wa.me/447886779958\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Whatsapp</a>.</p><p>Email is: <a href=\\\"mailto:info@circumcisioninlondon.co.uk\\\">info@circumcisioninlondon.co.uk</a><br><a href=\\\"tel:07886779958\\\">07886779958</a></p>\",\"eyebrow\":\"Talk to us\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book online\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/book/\",\"phoneLabel\":\"Call 020 8951 3794\",\"phoneUrl\":\"tel:+442089513794\",\"cardTitle\":\"\",\"cardHtml\":\"\",\"cardEyebrow\":\"Request a call back\",\"showCallback\":true,\"formId\":\"home\",\"formSubject\":\"homepage callback\",\"callbackAnchor\":\"request-callback\",\"nameLabel\":\"Your name\",\"phoneFieldLabel\":\"Phone number\",\"dobLabel\":\"Patient DOB\",\"messageLabel\":\"Anything you would like us to know\",\"optionalLabel\":\"(optional)\",\"consentHtml\":\"I am happy for the clinic to contact me about this enquiry. We do not add you to a mailing list. See our <a href=\\\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/privacy-notice/\\\" style=\\\"color:var(--blue-deep)\\\">privacy notice</a>.\",\"submitLabel\":\"Request a call back\",\"invalidMessage\":\"Please complete the highlighted field.\",\"sentMessage\":\"Opening your email app so this reaches the clinic. If nothing happens, call 020 8951 3794.\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/faq {\"heading\":\"The questions we are asked most\",\"items\":[{\"q\":\"Is the circumcision painful?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eNo. Every patient has local anaesthetic, at every age. It is safe, and it is illegal to circumcise without it.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe do not simply assume it has worked. Once it has had time, we test the area and show you that no pain is felt, and we only begin once you tell us you are happy to proceed. Babies sometimes cry anyway: the anaesthetic removes pain but keeps ordinary touch sensation, which is painless, and an unfamiliar touch there is enough to make a baby object.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"How long does it take?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor a baby, the circumcision itself is about ten minutes, and the anaesthetic lasts around two hours afterwards. Older children and adults take longer. Allow about an hour for the visit either way, which covers the consultation, consent, the anaesthetic working and going through aftercare before you leave.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Which method do you use?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor babies and toddlers, we often use the ring method (e.g. Plastibell or Circumplast). The advantages are that it does not require any stitches, you can bath your son normally and often comes off by itself within 3-14 days similar to the umbilical cord. The disadvantages is that it sometimes does not come off automatically and will require us to remove it but this often takes less than 5 seconds.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOlder children and adults are often circumcised with the forceps guided (traditional) method using thermal cautery which seals as it cuts, resulting in minimal bleeding if any. We close the wound using skin glue, stitches or a combination of both depending on the individual patient. Both of these come off naturally.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"What is the best age?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eUnder one month old, if the choice is open to you. At that age it is quick and simple and healing is faster. We circumcise routinely at every age after that, right through to adults, so it is never too late.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you carry out religious circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes, and it is a large part of what we do. Our Muslim practitioners carry out the procedure according to the Sunnah, and we routinely cater for all faiths and backgrounds. \\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/religious/\\u0022\\u003eMore about religious and cultural circumcision\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can you correct a circumcision done elsewhere?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Parents bring sons to us from across the UK and from abroad to tidy up work done somewhere else, and adults come for the same reason. It ranges from scar revision to tightening a loose result. \\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/re-circumcision/\\u0022\\u003eMore about re-circumcision\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do I need to do anything to prepare?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eVery little, because it is done under local anaesthetic. There is no fasting. When you book we send you videos on how to prepare and what to expect from start to finish, and the page for your age group lists exactly what to bring.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Could the NHS do this instead?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWhere there is a medical need, yes, and if you can wait that is a reasonable choice. From what our patients tell us, the wait runs beyond a year. Religious and cultural circumcision is not funded. Give us a call if you would like to discuss further.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
}
